# Upstream: giac 2.1.0 gen.cc sym_add, sym_sub, rdiv and rpn.cc _division: when one operand is an MPFR float (or a complex with MPFR parts) and the other has a float value, the other is brought to its precision with accurate_evalf and the operation called again if the result is_approx. For a vector is_approx means has_num_coeff (one float entry), and accurate_evalf leaves a symbolic constant symbolic (exp(1) becomes exp(1.0)), so a vector holding a float and exp(1), sqrt(2), ln(2) or sin(1) came back unchanged and the call repeated until the stack overflowed (RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded in the wasm build): [0.1,exp(1)]/2, [0.1,exp(1)]/2.0, 2.0/[0.1,exp(1)], [0.1,exp(1)]+2.0, [0.1,exp(1)]-2.0, 2.0-[0.1,exp(1)], [0.1,exp(1)]+(2.0+3.0*i) at Digits > 14, where a typed decimal is an MPFR float; so [[0.1,exp(1),pi],[5,2,7],[exp(1),7,9.81]]/10^4 killed the engine (Digits 12, doubles, took another case). Now a vector counts as converted only when every entry is a number (is_fully_numeric); otherwise the callers go on with has_evalf's value, as they do for a symbolic scalar. sym_mult (its vector case ends the recursion) is unchanged.
# Changed by Pascaline contributors, 2026-11-25
